0\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0015\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00d0\u0001\u0018\b\u00f6\u00ff\u00e6\u0000R\u0001The Bulldog was an attempt to make a big brother to the very sucessful Maddog OmniMec"
    },
    {
      "type": "ascii",
      "start": 802,
      "end": 1055,
      "text": "h, known in the Inner Sphere as the Hagateka, or Vulture.   Though the design was a marginal success, updating the chassis to 75 tons, some critics feel this design is merely a stopgap in attempt to fill holes in the still recovering Clan Forces.   \r\n\r\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "len_string",
      "start": 1055,
      "end": 1496,
      "length": 439,
      "text": "The final known variant of the Bulldog relies on The Advanced Tactical Missles as its Primary ammunition weapon, complimented by the long range kick of the two arm mounted extended range PPCs.  Three Anti-Missle Systems perch on this mech, though with only one ton of ammo, they run out quickly in battle.  \r\n\r\nThe Missle systems carry a ton of ammo of each kind for each rack, making it two tons of HE, two of ER and two tons of standard."
    },
